#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128867 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd4abd5d-2642-5f0d-af2f-5ed5c265526a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/id #uuid "2b2f2b8e-4625-5550-bb37-5ab9ca409c50" :question/math-academy-id "e-5032" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{2x+20}[/math]}} \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+12x+25\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-\\,\\,8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{20x+25}[/math]}} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{20x-80}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,105 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+20 \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+12x+25\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}-\\,\\,8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20x+25 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{20x-80}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,105 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are $2x+20$ and $20x+25.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128868 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/id #uuid "bda2e91a-5b55-5deb-8232-7e79fabf6f29" :question/math-academy-id "e-5033" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{x^2 - x + 1}[/math]}} \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+0x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}-x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{\\text{[math]\\phantom{x + 64}[/math]}} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,63\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x^2$-term and the $x$-term. So, we write it using zero coefficients, as follows:\n\n$$\nx^3+{\\color{red}0}x^2 + {\\color{red}0}x + 64\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-x+1 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+64\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,{x}^{2}+0x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,{x}^{2}-x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x+64 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x+1}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,63\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\qquad$ $x^2 - x + 1\\quad$ and $\\quad x + 64.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128870 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/id #uuid "e3e171d1-4428-5a4d-a050-5ad8eb843aff" :question/math-academy-id "e-5110" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-2 \\\\  & x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+8x-5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, what is $\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5}?$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-2 \\\\  & x+5\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,2{x}^{2}+8x-5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{2}+10x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-2x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $2x^2+8x -5$ by the linear binomial ${\\color{purple}x+5}$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${\\color{blue}2x-2},$ and\n\n- the remainder ${\\color{red}5}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+8x-5}{x+5} = {\\color{blue}2x-2}+\\dfrac{\\color{red}5}{\\color{purple}x+5}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd4abd5d-2642-5f0d-af2f-5ed5c265526a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8880d8d2-c546-5a02-a342-2b0309748345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x + 2$ and $6x - 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125841} {:answer/id #uuid "9d026acc-402d-5ba4-a2d1-59f7eded970a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x + 1$ and $6x - 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125842} {:answer/id #uuid "a5742d09-1d55-54ea-b38b-cfa5222464ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x + 2$ and $3x - 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125843} {:answer/id #uuid "e66c9f3c-f44c-5fa8-b731-b605012eb43a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x + 2$ and $6x - 1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125844} {:answer/id #uuid "77906cf5-bbd3-569c-82f9-08b29a951c02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x + 1$ and $3x - 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8880d8d2-c546-5a02-a342-2b0309748345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x + 2$ and $6x - 2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125841} :answer-field/id #uuid "d21484d9-53a1-5334-8f12-7d40e0bdedd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc20fe72-fd9e-5995-979a-b8ac4079769c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104126" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 3x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+4x+3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+2 \\\\  & 3x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+4x+3\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+3 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6x-2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $2x+2\\,$ and $\\,6x-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ddc1dd26-c9c3-575f-b07d-a223c7c888f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3} - 1 + \\frac{26}{x - 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125859} {:answer/id #uuid "e087d209-2752-580b-83c5-8495c371911e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + 3x + 9 + \\frac{26}{x - 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125860} {:answer/id #uuid "e5951ffc-5cf4-5db2-b1a0-0b3602821891" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26 + \\frac{x^{2} + 3x + 9}{x - 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125861} {:answer/id #uuid "e6f52fa5-3ee7-503b-9681-d5e509fa084a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26 + \\frac{x - 3}{x^{2} + 3x + 9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125862} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b5252c-55bb-5b2d-a2f2-dc6e58b7779e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - 3 + \\frac{26}{x^{2} + 3x + 9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e087d209-2752-580b-83c5-8495c371911e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + 3x + 9 + \\frac{26}{x - 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125860} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf831a4f-08b3-5065-a2b3-e043937ba32e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e43a33da-a50a-56f5-8fb4-57e6714e7429" :question/math-academy-id "q-104218" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+3x+9 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{9x-27}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{{x}^{3}-1}{x-3}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+3x+9 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,9x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{9x-27}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial ${x}^{3}-1$ by the linear binomial $x-3$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${x}^{2}+3x+9,$ and\n\n- the remainder $26.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}-1}{x-3}={x}^{2}+3x+9+\\frac{26}{x-3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa81dedb-5075-5f8d-a639-90ed6f4c19d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x - 10$ and $-20x + 25$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125865} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e20402-9d18-5d53-abf2-ed0110643826" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x - 10$ and $-10x + 95$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125866} {:answer/id #uuid "d23fa581-b656-55fb-a797-2f04f66bf841" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x + 5$ and $-20x - 100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125867} {:answer/id #uuid "1e09835d-38c0-5baf-b4af-320d0cc39770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x + 5$ and $-20x + 25$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125868} {:answer/id #uuid "3587d93c-e3c2-5c58-89a3-e48d4075c076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x - 10$ and $-20x - 100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3587d93c-e3c2-5c58-89a3-e48d4075c076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x - 10$ and $-20x - 100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125869} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9009979-cf99-5ef3-ad94-a8cdbcd017a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186125864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a350b09f-4988-53e2-ac83-0f8cea3d1cc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-104226" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 2x+10\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x-5} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+20x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-20x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,95\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+0x-5\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-10 \\\\  & 2x+10\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+0x-5} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+20x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-20x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,20x-100}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,95\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $2x-10\\,$ and $\\,-20x-100.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331767 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd4abd5d-2642-5f0d-af2f-5ed5c265526a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d95c195b-e445-5e41-b0e3-8007f8ec3c2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11{x}^{2}-10x+28\\,$ and $\\,10{x}^{2}+12x+14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331769} {:answer/id #uuid "12dc4dce-da1d-51dd-b557-2472505df2bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11{x}^{2}-20x-28\\,$ and $\\,20{x}^{2}-12x-14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331770} {:answer/id #uuid "df0cddf9-56d1-56ba-a204-ad5166bbd863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11{x}^{2}+10x+33\\,$ and $\\,10{x}^{2}+13x-14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331771} {:answer/id #uuid "f5222a89-3a2d-52fb-ac9a-41387f691d48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11{x}^{2}+20x-28\\,$ and $\\,20{x}^{2}-12x+14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331772} {:answer/id #uuid "817100aa-4b8b-52ac-abbd-9ad29c8c8a69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11{x}^{2}-10x+33\\,$ and $\\,-10{x}^{2}+13x+14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df0cddf9-56d1-56ba-a204-ad5166bbd863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$11{x}^{2}+10x+33\\,$ and $\\,10{x}^{2}+13x-14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331771} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fddfa8c-9672-5b0a-be81-efca2775913a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331768}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da0e8dd9-41a3-5bce-a1c9-a30667cb7951" :question/math-academy-id "q-105589" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,11{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+13x-14\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{11{x}^{3}-22{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{10{x}^{2}-20x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,33x-14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{33x-66}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,52\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,11{x}^{2}+10x+33 \\\\  & x-2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,11{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+13x-14\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{11{x}^{3}-22{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,10{x}^{2}+13x-14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{10{x}^{2}-20x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,33x-14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{33x-66}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,52\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $11{x}^{2}+10x+33\\,$ and $\\,10{x}^{2}+13x-14.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331774 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd4abd5d-2642-5f0d-af2f-5ed5c265526a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcca42af-6482-5d6e-9208-f0b83878edb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-2x+1\\,$ and $\\,-3{x}^{2}+x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331776} {:answer/id #uuid "f64dae68-6e5d-56a4-9250-7844e06181f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}+x+2\\,$ and $\\,+3{x}^{2}-x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331777} {:answer/id #uuid "c2120c1c-e3e6-5b11-a9c3-4eb9325a5686" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-x+2\\,$ and $\\,-3{x}^{2}+x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331778} {:answer/id #uuid "5f26f7ff-effb-5be6-a177-3392e823d595" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}+2x+1\\,$ and $\\,6{x}^{2}+x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331779} {:answer/id #uuid "9eec8e59-687a-57ab-832f-ebf40835baac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-2x+2\\,$ and $\\,-6{x}^{2}+x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2120c1c-e3e6-5b11-a9c3-4eb9325a5686" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-x+2\\,$ and $\\,-3{x}^{2}+x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331778} :answer-field/id #uuid "f48803f8-0e7e-5ba0-ac75-2761a3a78391" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43288d06-2433-5fb0-a435-3396899a6f12" :question/math-academy-id "q-105591" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 3x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{6{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+7x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,3{x}^{2}+7x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6x-2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-x+2 \\\\  & 3x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{6{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+7x+4\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,3{x}^{2}+7x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,3{x}^{2}+\\,\\,x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6x-2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $2{x}^{2}-x+2\\,$ and $\\,-3{x}^{2}+x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd4abd5d-2642-5f0d-af2f-5ed5c265526a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3384283a-f70e-50c1-b859-18f1b221804a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4{x}^{2}+10x+55\\,$ and $\\,9{x}^{2}+2x-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331783} {:answer/id #uuid "81e34ca6-435c-5f9c-a994-6a45d3c57d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4{x}^{2}+11x+45\\,$ and $\\,11{x}^{2}+x-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331784} {:answer/id #uuid "b4bd19f3-9382-564c-adcb-53034186157e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4{x}^{2}+11x-35\\,$ and $\\,11{x}^{2}-x-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331785} {:answer/id #uuid "fbb2e4f3-c449-5c92-b535-aab50b1c4c36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4{x}^{2}+10x+45\\,$ and $\\,11{x}^{2}-x-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331786} {:answer/id #uuid "59237a01-aad1-5e50-ba02-6a6eb3530353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4{x}^{2}-11x+45\\,$ and $\\,11{x}^{2}-2x-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81e34ca6-435c-5f9c-a994-6a45d3c57d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4{x}^{2}+11x+45\\,$ and $\\,11{x}^{2}+x-5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331784} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6134135-9df8-5c4b-9198-fd0edbb02801" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fb3fd947-7e73-5d82-83d8-1c4c922146ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-113746" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-4\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+x-5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{11{x}^{2}-44x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,45x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{45x-180}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,175\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+11x+45 \\\\  & x-4\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}+x-5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,11{x}^{2}+x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{11{x}^{2}-44x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,45x-5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{45x-180}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,175\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $4{x}^{2}+11x+45\\,$ and $\\,11{x}^{2}+x-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331788 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7acdb856-a60d-546c-a1eb-8d0750f5e418" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-1+\\frac{5}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331790} {:answer/id #uuid "368678fd-cdc1-5dde-814c-ed4cea0ea279" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+3-\\frac{1}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331791} {:answer/id #uuid "40ef858d-ce93-5a7a-8b4e-292c45060809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-3-\\frac{3}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331792} {:answer/id #uuid "063beb81-4a94-5c9d-a6de-ff043516cec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-2+\\frac{1}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331793} {:answer/id #uuid "b25ddf86-f7fe-5c5b-9080-1ca2ba9f01e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-5-\\frac{2}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40ef858d-ce93-5a7a-8b4e-292c45060809" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x-3-\\frac{3}{x+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331792} :answer-field/id #uuid "f476abc9-7435-5a5b-a467-d0c5fabddbf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331789}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "721dc8b5-0c4e-5c7d-b5a9-6627d3e8e1db" :question/math-academy-id "q-113827" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x-3 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,5{x}^{2}+2x-6\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5{x}^{2}+5x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3x-6 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-3x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{5{x}^{2}+2x-6}{x+1}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x-3 \\\\  & x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,5{x}^{2}+2x-6\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5{x}^{2}+5x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3x-6 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-3x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $5{x}^{2}+2x-6$ by the linear binomial $x+1$ gives\n\n- the quotient $5x-3,$ and\n\n- the remainder $-3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{x}^{2}+2x-6}{x+1}=5x-3-\\frac{3}{x+1}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331795 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b97b39da-035e-5025-98cd-aad9a8f6d12e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+48\\,$ and $\\,48x-8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331797} {:answer/id #uuid "c5b7577e-41df-517b-8390-357ccd512d9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x-24\\,$ and $\\,24x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331798} {:answer/id #uuid "501d83cb-89e3-5346-b6b5-c842130b0412" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+30\\,$ and $\\,30x-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331799} {:answer/id #uuid "b254bc39-624a-53d0-af90-095fd3948c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x-36\\,$ and $\\,48x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331800} {:answer/id #uuid "491186b9-9d6f-57d3-9096-4df6e5140098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "491186b9-9d6f-57d3-9096-4df6e5140098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331801} :answer-field/id #uuid "424ef1ac-66b8-5c64-8fb2-4d17ef24ef56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331796}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3536c096-9c19-5ecb-8cd6-bf3a33c8475e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114262" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-4} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-36x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{36x-216}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,212\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows: \n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+0x-4\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+36 \\\\  & x-6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-4} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-36x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,36x-4 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{36x-216}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,212\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $6x+36\\,$ and $\\,36x-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331802 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b314669-ff86-5107-8d01-40f4bab1dc10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}^{2}-4x+6\\,$ and $\\,8{x}^{2}-15x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331804} {:answer/id #uuid "2478f688-4233-5395-a8bb-99eaf7c3b2c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}^{2}+4x+4\\,$ and $\\,8{x}^{2}-10x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331805} {:answer/id #uuid "1c4948d4-290d-5b28-8106-77aa70068141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}^{2}-2x+3\\,$ and $\\,-8{x}^{2}-12x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331806} {:answer/id #uuid "f05b14b9-44a0-534c-9e8d-62503e3e1fda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}^{2}-8x+5\\,$ and $\\,-6{x}^{2}-4x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331807} {:answer/id #uuid "31b9b86d-390c-5fd7-9e81-6e1218192e2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}^{2}-6x+3\\,$ and $\\,-6{x}^{2}-8x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c4948d4-290d-5b28-8106-77aa70068141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${x}^{2}-2x+3\\,$ and $\\,-8{x}^{2}-12x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331806} :answer-field/id #uuid "d083392a-d05b-543c-8bd4-c59dc28a6e6b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331803}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "252c7219-93b7-53af-acf7-f0168872d045" :question/math-academy-id "q-114266" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 4x+6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+0x+8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,8{x}^{2}+0x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,12x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{12x+18}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,10\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n4{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+0x+8\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}-2x+3 \\\\  & 4x+6\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,4{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+0x+8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,8{x}^{2}+0x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,8{x}^{2}-12x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,12x+8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{12x+18}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ ${x}^{2}-2x+3\\,$ and $\\,-8{x}^{2}-12x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331809 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a95b865-4828-5dea-a10d-ccc83499dea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331811} {:answer/id #uuid "90082a3e-89bf-5853-8cbb-d2b243dc711b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90082a3e-89bf-5853-8cbb-d2b243dc711b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331812} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ca4e512-1bea-5a9c-ae60-dfa66b9f7d29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331810} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c028963-784d-5ecb-a839-90be5cec35b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c028963-784d-5ecb-a839-90be5cec35b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331814} :answer-field/id #uuid "515e06f0-9957-5618-81ec-5da5cd88311d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0dd8a252-fb1f-53b3-92e6-39fb1930bb1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-320860" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+4 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-5x-10\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x-10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4x-12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we conclude the following:\n\n| $3{x}^{2}-5x-10$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} | $+\\,\\,$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x-3$ |  | $x-3$ |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+4 \\\\  & x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-5x-10\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-9x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x-10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4x-12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $3{x}^{2}-5x-10$ by the linear binomial $x-3$ gives\n\n- the quotient $3x+4,$ and\n\n- the remainder $2.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}-5x-10}{x-3}=3x+4+\\frac{2}{x-3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331815 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26b3d08e-1a22-5281-84a8-ec95dd0fa0aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^2-x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331817} {:answer/id #uuid "fabf741e-f3b3-5813-9a69-999334200609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^2+x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26b3d08e-1a22-5281-84a8-ec95dd0fa0aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^2-x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331817} :answer-field/id #uuid "792146d0-d948-5d51-8c34-3d6f42fcc8be" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dc625e0b-ba1a-54ee-a747-0aeb62165cd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc625e0b-ba1a-54ee-a747-0aeb62165cd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331820} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d867463-0ba6-54a3-8644-5164ac3f4cea" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ae68684-3d32-56dc-9978-f459734a53fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-320865" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-x+4 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+2x+2\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+2x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-{x}^{2}-2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4x+8}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, we conclude the following:\n\n| $3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+2x+2$ | $=$ | {{field-1}} | $-\\,\\,$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+2$ |  | $x+2$ |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-x+4 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+2x+2\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}+2x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-{x}^{2}-2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4x+2 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4x+8}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+2x+2$ by the linear binomial $x+2$ gives\n\n- the quotient $3{x}^{2}-x+4,$ and\n\n- the remainder $-6.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}+5{x}^{2}+2x+2}{x+2}=3{x}^{2}-x+4-\\frac{6}{x+2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331821 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd4abd5d-2642-5f0d-af2f-5ed5c265526a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6878cce-00cb-511c-88a4-c8f76affc770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x+4\\,$ and $\\,28x-12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331823} {:answer/id #uuid "f610e6d8-8230-50c4-b013-735be2f6b5cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x-4\\,$ and $\\,28x-12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331824} {:answer/id #uuid "4e6cc4ee-8057-5ed0-b755-4697e3e8a37a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x+2\\,$ and $\\,14x-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331825} {:answer/id #uuid "90fb31fe-a60f-545c-84f3-37d8761e66e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x-1\\,$ and $\\,-7x+3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331826} {:answer/id #uuid "f0611e3c-fee8-5c19-b2ef-096150f57057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x+1\\,$ and $\\,7x-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6878cce-00cb-511c-88a4-c8f76affc770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x+4\\,$ and $\\,28x-12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331823} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a6e7d43-6192-5883-8a4a-ae9fa6224f66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0878edad-fdb3-558c-86e5-de500beaa6d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-37860" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 7x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,14{x}^{2}+22x-12\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{14{x}^{2}-\\,\\,6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{28x-12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x+4 \\\\  & 7x-3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,14{x}^{2}+22x-12\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{14{x}^{2}-\\,\\,6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,28x-12 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{28x-12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0 \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $2x+4\\,$ and $\\,28x-12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331828 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5afd13c-5860-526f-9136-7cc2b65da03d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3{x}^{2}+3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3x-3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331830} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5df092-7dd1-5cdf-84a4-7dae6bbdcc30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3{x}^{2}-3x+1\\,$ and $\\,3x+3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331831} {:answer/id #uuid "0639961b-0b65-53d4-9385-192def894e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3{x}^{2}+x-3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}-3x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331832} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff853e2-c415-531a-aab1-0480387a5f68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3{x}^{2}-3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}+3x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331833} {:answer/id #uuid "6760fafb-634b-5cc5-a3d9-cd3be0642953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3{x}^{2}+3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}-3x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6760fafb-634b-5cc5-a3d9-cd3be0642953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3{x}^{2}+3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}-3x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331834} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb773819-93bd-5ba9-a5ee-2c6746b4d64e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331829}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f2beb0d-f178-5844-a215-15b69fb958ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-37977" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$-term and the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n3{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+5\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+3x+3 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,3{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x+5\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}+0x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3{x}^{2}-3x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+5 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x-3}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $3{x}^{2}+3x+3\\,$ and $\\,3{x}^{2}-3x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331835 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e301f552-6a28-58c5-90bc-3f8798d79118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+8x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331837} {:answer/id #uuid "0ed17c77-f314-5a7d-a80f-ec09ec07f449" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+8x+2+\\frac{2}{x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331838} {:answer/id #uuid "775594a7-038e-5f78-ba93-f99e1c52ead2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+8x+2-\\frac{1}{x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331839} {:answer/id #uuid "847257d7-9bb4-5d52-92f5-4360f5b9f2d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+8x-2+\\frac{1}{x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331840} {:answer/id #uuid "89a7b1e7-8b7c-5734-a358-c1237e32f680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+8x+2+\\frac{1}{x-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e301f552-6a28-58c5-90bc-3f8798d79118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+8x+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331837} :answer-field/id #uuid "43b96372-69a4-53cb-9f33-eadf9d5f9c22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "571834c6-f07f-578b-b816-e7ff7991f3a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-38049" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+8x+2 \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}-30x-8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8{x}^{2}-30x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{8{x}^{2}-32x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2x-8}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{6{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}-30x-8}{x-4}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+8x+2 \\\\  & x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}-30x-8\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8{x}^{2}-30x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{8{x}^{2}-32x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-8 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2x-8}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $6{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}-30x-8$ by the linear binomial $x-4$ gives\n\n- the quotient $6{x}^{2}+8x+2,$ and\n\n- the remainder $0.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{6{x}^{3}-16{x}^{2}-30x-8}{x-4}=6{x}^{2}+8x+2+\\frac{0}{x-4}=6{x}^{2}+8x+2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331842 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "489a6abd-3eae-59f9-8825-093f96f4f738" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x-4\\,$ and $\\,-4x-16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331844} {:answer/id #uuid "bd788b47-ffeb-5054-9d8d-e6078e1d10ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x+4\\,$ and $\\,4x-16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331845} {:answer/id #uuid "0bbb58ff-1b36-5c45-986f-253a83689e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x-1\\,$ and $\\,-x+4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331846} {:answer/id #uuid "b880834f-0b10-5dcf-a262-a0ce128e33c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x+4\\,$ and $\\,4x+16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331847} {:answer/id #uuid "e7da4576-a16d-590f-be62-5855d8a540a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x-4\\,$ and $\\,-4x+16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7da4576-a16d-590f-be62-5855d8a540a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x-4\\,$ and $\\,-4x+16$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331848} :answer-field/id #uuid "570c101d-bc4a-5bc4-8ceb-c63399a346eb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "97a67cfa-cbb4-5ac8-9bbc-80fac24ef619" :question/math-academy-id "q-38108" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x+16} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4x-16}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+0x+16\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-4 \\\\  & x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x+16} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,4x+16 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4x-16}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $x-4\\,$ and $\\,-4x+16.$"}]}
